---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Lutaro - Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Lutaro, the Sony camera Picture Profile manager for iOS, iPadOS, and macOS."
>
  <h1>Lutaro Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="meta">Effective 2 July 2026</p>

  <p>
    Lutaro is an app for managing Sony camera Picture Profiles and Creative
    Looks on iPhone, iPad, and Mac.
    <strong>Lutaro collects no data about you.</strong> There are no accounts,
    no analytics, no tracking, no ads, and no servers of ours. Nothing you do
    in the app is sent to us or to anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>Data we collect</h2>
  <p>
    None. Lutaro has no analytics or tracking of any kind. The app never
    sends anything to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Your profile library</h2>
  <p>
    The profiles, tags, and preview images you create stay on your device. If
    you turn on iCloud, the library can sync through <em>your own</em> iCloud
    account. Apple handles that data under
    <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a>.
    We never see it.
  </p>

  <h2>Camera connections and credentials</h2>
  <p>
    Lutaro talks directly to your camera, over your Wi-Fi network or over a
    USB cable. A USB connection uses no network at all: the app talks to the
    camera through the cable and sends nothing anywhere else.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your camera password is kept in the device Keychain. Connection details,
    such as the camera's name, stay on your device. The app sends your user
    name and password to your camera only, never anywhere else.
  </p>

  <h2>Local network access</h2>
  <p>
    The app asks for local-network permission only to find and connect to
    your camera on your Wi-Fi network. It does not scan for, connect to, or
    collect anything about other devices.
  </p>

  <h2>Photo library access</h2>
  <p>
    If you choose a sample image for a profile, the app reads only the photo
    you pick. It never browses or uploads your photo library.
  </p>

  <h2>Diagnostics</h2>
  <p>
    Lutaro can create a diagnostics report to help fix camera connection
    problems. A report is only made when you ask for one. Network addresses
    and serial numbers are hidden by default, and nothing leaves your device
    unless you send it yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes in an important way, we will publish the new
    version at this address with a new date.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or concerns? Email
    <a href="mailto:lutaro@akitaka.me">lutaro@akitaka.me</a>, or open an issue at
    <a href="https://github.com/tarakanof/Lutaro-Site/issues">github.com/tarakanof/Lutaro-Site/issues</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
